   "source": [
    "## Individual-stock time-series regressions: MKT, LMH, and joint models\n",
    "\n",
    "Each stock's monthly excess returns are regressed on three specifications: market excess return only (MKT), low-minus-high idiosyncratic-volatility return only (LMH = Q1 - Q5), and both factors together. The model estimates the intercept and each included beta, with Newey-West/HAC standard errors (six lags), two-sided normal-approximation p-values, and 95% confidence intervals. Each model uses that stock's available months with the required factors and requires at least 36 observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The significance summary reports the eligible-stock count and share with significant factor loadings separately by model and factor. LMH is formed from portfolios in the same stock universe, so its loadings are descriptive, not an independent out-of-sample test. Results are not adjusted for multiple testing."
   ]
  },
