    "## Fama-MacBeth factor pricing\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook estimates three independent two-pass factor-pricing models for stock excess returns:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **MKT only:** estimate and price market beta alone.\n",
    "- **LMH only:** estimate and price LMH beta alone.\n",
    "- **MKT + LMH:** estimate and price both betas jointly.\n",
    "\n",
<<<<<<< HEAD
    "Let `R_{i,t}` be stock *i*'s total return, `RF_t` the risk-free return, `MKT_t = R_{M,t} - RF_t` the market excess return, and `LMH_t = Q1_t - Q5_t` the equal-weighted low-minus-high idiosyncratic-volatility portfolio return. The dependent variable in all three models is the stock's excess return, `R_{i,t} - RF_t`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**First pass (time-series beta estimation):** for each stock, estimate betas using the trailing 60 monthly observations ending before month *t* (requiring at least 36 valid observations). The standard CAPM estimates market beta only:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,s} - RF_s = a_i + \\beta_{M,i} MKT_s + \\varepsilon_{i,s}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The joint-factor specification estimates market and LMH betas together:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,s} - RF_s = a_i + \\beta_{M,i} MKT_s + \\beta_{LMH,i} LMH_s + \\varepsilon_{i,s},$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and the LMH-only specification is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,s} - RF_s = a_i + \\beta_{LMH,i} LMH_s + \\varepsilon_{i,s}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Second pass (monthly cross-sectional pricing):** each month *t*, regress that month's stock excess returns on the betas estimated using only earlier data. The standard CAPM model is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,t} - RF_t = \\lambda_{0,t} + \\lambda_{M,t}\\widehat{\\beta}_{M,i,t} + u_{i,t}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The joint-factor model is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,t} - RF_t = \\lambda_{0,t} + \\lambda_{M,t}\\widehat{\\beta}_{M,i,t} + \\lambda_{LMH,t}\\widehat{\\beta}_{LMH,i,t} + u_{i,t},$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and the LMH-only model is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R_{i,t} - RF_t = \\lambda_{0,t} + \\lambda_{LMH,t}\\widehat{\\beta}_{LMH,i,t} + u_{i,t}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The reported Fama-MacBeth risk prices are the time-series averages of the monthly `lambda` coefficients; their standard errors use Newey-West/HAC with six lags. The LMH exposure null is **H0: mean(`lambda_LMH,t`) = 0**; the market exposure null is **H0: mean(`lambda_M,t`) = 0**. `lambda_{0,t}` is the second-pass intercept, not the LMH portfolio's time-series CAPM alpha. For each second-pass model, outputs report average cross-sectional R-squared and adjusted R-squared across months as measures of model fit; these fit statistics are distinct from the tests of whether average risk prices are zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "The factor-return correlation and variance inflation factor (VIF) are also reported to assess collinearity between MKT and LMH.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to read the output tables.** The standard CAPM table reports the intercept and market risk price from a model whose only factor is market excess return. The joint-model table reports average monthly prices of MKT and LMH exposure; the LMH-only table reports the intercept and LMH risk price without a market-beta control. All report HAC inference and average cross-sectional R-squared measures. The multicollinearity table reports the MKT-LMH return correlation and VIF; larger absolute correlation or VIF means more overlapping factor variation, which can make individual coefficient estimates less precise. The MKT-LMH correlation is about -0.60 and VIF about 1.57, indicating some overlap but not severe multicollinearity."
